    "updated_at": "2025-02-28T14:31:56Z",
    "body": "I'm implementing actions in Firefox and I find it impractical to retrieve the actual max number of actions via a synchronous attribute, on top of the fingerprinting concern mentioned here.\n\n[Chrome returns 2 everywhere](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/public/common/notifications/notification_constants.h;l=20;drc=58fb75d86a0ad2642beec2d6c16b1e6c008e33cd), Firefox will most probably do the same. Maybe the spec can also just define it as constant.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
