    "updated_at": "2025-03-18T16:39:33Z",
    "body": "Just to note: Currently platforms do not provide an API for browsers to query about the max action count. It's all hardcoded: [Android says 3](https://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/Notification.Builder.html#addAction(android.app.Notification.Action)), [Windows says 5](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/uwp/schemas/tiles/toastschema/element-actions), and [macOS says 10](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/usernotifications/unnotificationcategory?language=objc), and not even sure whether it's documented at all for Gnome/KDE/other Linux desktop environments. And all of these may be different based on their versions.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
